==English==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|en|ten}}
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|detenir}}. Cognate with {{cog|it|detenere}}, {{cog|pt|deter}}, {{cog|ro|deține}}, and {{cog|es|detener}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/dɪˈteɪn/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-detain.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪn}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To keep someone from [[proceed]]ing by [[hold back|holding them back]] or making [[claim]]s on their [[attention]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To put under [[custody]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To keep back or from; to withhold.
#* {{RQ:Taylor HL}}
#*: '''Detain''' not the wages of the hireling.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[seize]] [[goods]] for [[official]] [[purpose]]s.

